#: ../../../cmake-modules/targetLinkLibrariesWithDynamicLookup.rst:2
msgid "targetLinkLibrariesWithDynamicLookup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/targetLinkLibrariesWithDynamicLookup.cmake:4
msgid "Public Functions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/targetLinkLibrariesWithDynamicLookup.cmake:6
msgid "The following functions are defined:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/targetLinkLibrariesWithDynamicLookup.cmake:12
msgid "target_link_libraries_with_dynamic_lookup(<Target> [<Libraries>])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/targetLinkLibrariesWithDynamicLookup.cmake:15
msgid ""
"Useful to \"weakly\" link a loadable module. For example, it should be used "
"when compiling a loadable module when the symbols should be resolve from the "
"run-time environment where the module is loaded, and not a specific system "
"library."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/targetLinkLibrariesWithDynamicLookup.cmake:20
msgid ""
"Like proper linking, except that the given ``<Libraries>`` are not "
"necessarily linked. Instead, the ``<Target>`` is produced in a manner that "
"allows for symbols unresolved within it to be resolved at runtime, "
"presumably by the given ``<Libraries>``.  If such a target can be produced, "
"the provided ``<Libraries>`` are not actually linked."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/targetLinkLibrariesWithDynamicLookup.cmake:26
msgid ""
"It links a library to a target such that the symbols are resolved at run-"
"time not link-time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/targetLinkLibrariesWithDynamicLookup.cmake:29
msgid ""
"The linker is checked to see if it supports undefined symbols when linking a "
"shared library. If it does then the library is not linked when specified "
"with this function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/targetLinkLibrariesWithDynamicLookup.cmake:33
msgid ""
"On platforms that do not support weak-linking, this function works just like "
"``target_link_libraries``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/targetLinkLibrariesWithDynamicLookup.cmake:38
msgid ""
"For OSX it uses ``undefined dynamic_lookup``. This is similar to using ``-"
"shared`` on Linux where undefined symbols are ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/targetLinkLibrariesWithDynamicLookup.cmake:41
msgid ""
"For more details, see `blog <http://blog.tim-smith.us/2015/09/python-"
"extension-modules-os-x/>`_ from Tim D. Smith."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/targetLinkLibrariesWithDynamicLookup.cmake:47
msgid ""
"Check if the linker requires a command line flag to allow leaving symbols "
"unresolved when producing a target of type ``<TargetType>`` that is weakly-"
"linked against a dependency of type ``<LibType>``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/targetLinkLibrariesWithDynamicLookup.cmake:51
msgid "``<TargetType>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/targetLinkLibrariesWithDynamicLookup.cmake:52
msgid "can be one of \"STATIC\", \"SHARED\", \"MODULE\", or \"EXE\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/targetLinkLibrariesWithDynamicLookup.cmake:54
msgid "``<LibType>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/targetLinkLibrariesWithDynamicLookup.cmake:55
msgid "can be one of \"STATIC\", \"SHARED\", or \"MODULE\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/targetLinkLibrariesWithDynamicLookup.cmake:57
msgid "Long signature:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/targetLinkLibrariesWithDynamicLookup.cmake:61
msgid ""
"check_dynamic_lookup(<TargetType>\n"
"                     <LibType>\n"
"                     <ResultVar>\n"
"                     [<LinkFlagsVar>])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/targetLinkLibrariesWithDynamicLookup.cmake:67
msgid "Short signature:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/targetLinkLibrariesWithDynamicLookup.cmake:71
msgid ""
"check_dynamic_lookup(<ResultVar>) # <TargetType> set to \"MODULE\"\n"
"                                  # <LibType> set to \"SHARED\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/targetLinkLibrariesWithDynamicLookup.cmake:75
msgid ""
"The result is cached between invocations and recomputed only when the value "
"of CMake's linker flag list changes; ``CMAKE_STATIC_LINKER_FLAGS`` if "
"``<TargetType>`` is \"STATIC\", and ``CMAKE_SHARED_LINKER_FLAGS`` otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/targetLinkLibrariesWithDynamicLookup.cmake:80
#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/targetLinkLibrariesWithDynamicLookup.cmake:128
#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/targetLinkLibrariesWithDynamicLookup.cmake:150
